# The paper reports no training-cost or inference-cost figures.

###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - PET is a new message-passing transformer that is not intrinsically equivariant; ECSE is a symmetrisation protocol applicable to any model. No derivation from a registry method is stated.
# - Table 1 labels the MnO errors RMSE, Table 4 MAE (0.30 meV, 22.7 meV/A for the same model); the Table 1 labelling is followed. The out-of-sample HEA25 errors of App. C.4 (300 K: 9.5 meV/atom and 0.13 eV/A; 5000 K: 152 meV/atom and 0.28 eV/A) do not name their statistic and are not encoded.
# - HME21 'MAE |f|' (140.5 meV/A, error on the force norm) is not encoded; the force-component MAE (124.0) is. Ensemble results (five models) are not encoded.
# - Liquid-water accuracy for other architectures and cutoffs is in Fig. 3 only. CH4 and QM9 dipole results are learning curves.
# - Data-set levels of theory are not described in this paper; COLL and HME21 split sizes are not restated.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/pozdnyakov2023.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.

